    "answer": {
      "short": "$xy=1$.",
      "worked": "The original logarithms require $x>0$ and $y>0$. Express all logarithms in base 2:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{3}\\log_2(x)+\\frac{1}{3}\\log_2(y)&=\\frac{1}{4}\\log_2(xy)\\\\\\frac{1}{3}\\log_2(xy)&=\\frac{1}{4}\\log_2(xy)\\\\\\frac{1}{12}\\log_2(xy)&=0\\\\\\log_2(xy)&=0\\\\xy&=2^0\\\\xy&=1.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
